# Independent smoke journal review

Reviewed implementation commit 12543b2 against doc/spec/15-site.md (especially the public smoke and bounded transaction contracts), the original payload/smoke/journal implementations, tests, and deployment README. No implementation was edited.

One blocking issue was found and fixed: with a 3600-second transaction budget, a report returning after 301 seconds was originally recorded remotely as SmokePassed despite the 300-second HTTP allowance. smoke-cap-repro.py/json preserve that original counterexample. The final implementation retains a separate observation deadline and rejects success at/after it, preserving the original report in SmokeFailed evidence.

Final independent validation: all 5 real-Git integration tests passed normally and under python -O (commands.json and raw stdout/stderr). Additional real-Git probes verified 301 seconds and exactly 300 seconds both persist SmokeFailed and raise; a timely HTTP pass followed by a successful but late remote push preserves SmokePassed evidence yet raises instead of returning success. recheck.json records the outcomes. Source snapshots match commit 12543b2 byte-for-byte.

No remaining blocking finding within this adapter scope. Exact local file closure, canonical tar digest, source identity, HTTPS base, expected API success history and remote head are checked before HTTP; report identity and evidence size are checked before append. Local CAS and normal remote push failures propagate. Re-entry after a smoke event requires reconciliation rather than treating its event as a fresh status history.

These tests use real temporary Git repositories and injected HTTP reports; they do not validate live Pages deployment, TLS, publisher lock/protection/eligibility, immutable recovery storage, LKG promotion, or rollback. The adapter records byte observations, not proof of current public deployment identity. Git/process creation and cleanup are not hard real-time operations. Full site suite and repository checks were run by the parent, not independently claimed here.
